{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a code generation pipeline task (#5572) to implement `cmd/pinky/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing srd098-pinky requirements R1.1, R1.2, and R1.3 — the short format (default) output for the pinky utility. Pinky is a lightweight finger information lookup tool that reads the utmpx database and passwd entries to display user login information. The implementation must follow the project's CGo utmpx pattern (as seen in cmd/users), include SIGPIPE handling, and compile cleanly. No git commands should be run — git is managed externally by the orchestrator.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - CGo integration for reading the utmpx database (C.setutxent, C.getutxent, C.endutxent)\n   - utmpx entry fields: ut_user, ut_line, ut_host, ut_tv, ut_type (USER_PROCESS filter)\n   - GECOS field parsing from passwd entries (for user real name, office, phone)\n   - Terminal idle time calculation (stat the /dev/tty device, compare mtime to now)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Differential testing against gpinky (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - Short format output: header line + one line per user with login, tty, idle, login time, host\n   - User filtering: when USER arguments given, show only those users\n   - The -s flag forces short format (which is already the default behavior)\n   - 40-line function size limit (E8), 500-line file size limit (E9), copyright header required\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd098-pinky.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining all pinky requirements. Only R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 are in scope for this task.\n     - R1.1: Short format default display (login name, terminal, idle time, login time, remote host)\n     - R1.2: USER arguments filter to show only specified users\n     - R1.3: -s forces short format (default behavior)\n     - Non-goals: does not read .plan or .project files on macOS\n     ```yaml\n     R1:\n       title: Short format (default)\n       items:\n         - R1.1:\n             text: Must display logged-in users in short format by default, showing login name, terminal, idle time, login time, and remote host, one line per user.\n         - R1.2:\n             text: When given USER arguments, must show information only for those users (from passwd and utmpx).\n         - R1.3:\n             text: \"-s must force short format output (default behavior).\"\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/users/main.go` (reference pattern for utmpx reading)\n     - Shows the CGo utmpx pattern to follow: C headers, setutxent/getutxent/endutxent loop, USER_PROCESS filtering\n     - Full file content (108 lines) read and available in conversation\n     - Key pattern - readUsers function:\n     ```go\n     func readUsers() []string {\n         C.setutxent()\n         defer C.endutxent()\n         var names []string\n         for {\n             entry := C.getutxent()\n             if entry == nil {\n                 break\n             }\n             if entry.ut_type != C.USER_PROCESS {\n                 continue\n             }\n             name := C.GoString(&entry.ut_user[0])\n             names = append(names, name)\n         }\n         return names\n     }\n     ```\n     - CGo import block pattern:\n     ```go\n     /*\n     #include <utmpx.h>\n     #include <stdlib.h>\n     */\n     import \"C\"\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - InstallSIGPIPEHandler() function to call at start of main\n     \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests for differential testing pattern\n     - BuildBinary helper for test compilation\n\n   - `cmd/pinky/main.go` — FILE TO CREATE\n     - Must implement R1.1, R1.2, R1.3 of srd098-pinky\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — implementation has not started. Only file reads were performed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand exact requirements for R1.1, R1.2, R1.3\n   - Read cmd/users/main.go to understand the CGo utmpx pattern to follow\n   - Identified that pinky short format needs: login name, terminal, idle time, login time, and remote host\n   - Identified that USER arguments require passwd lookup (for R1.2 — show info for specified users even if not logged in)\n   - Identified that idle time requires stat-ing the terminal device file\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification including role, repository files listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with required reading/files/requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement cmd/pinky/main.go with srd098 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/pinky/main.go` implementing srd098 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/pinky ./cmd/pinky/`\n   - Verify `go vet ./cmd/pinky/` passes with no warnings\n   - The task does NOT include creating a test file (pinky_test.go is not in the files list)\n   - The task does NOT include R2.x (long format, -f, -b, -h, -p flags) or R3.x (exit codes) beyond SIGPIPE\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the two required reference files (srd098-pinky.yaml and cmd/users/main.go) and was about to begin implementing cmd/pinky/main.go. No code has been written yet. The implementation needs to:\n   \n