{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RA9RnSW7aTJi9ZUFdF4K4d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// cmd/chown implements srd091-chown R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"errors\"\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"os/user\"\n12\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n13\t\t\"strconv\"\n14\t\t\"strings\"\n15\t\n16\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n17\t)\n18\t\n19\tconst helpText = `Usage: chown [OPTION]... [OWNER][:[GROUP]] FILE...\n20\t  or:  chown [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...\n21\tChange the owner and/or group of each FILE to OWNER and/or GROUP.\n22\t\n23\t  -c, --changes          like verbose but report only when a change is made\n24\t  -f, --silent, --quiet  suppress most error messages\n25\t  -v, --verbose          output a diagnostic for every file processed\n26\t      --dereference      affect the referent of each symbolic link (this is\n27\t                         the default), rather than the symbolic link itself\n28\t  -h, --no-dereference   affect symbolic links instead of any referenced file\n29\t      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially (the default)\n30\t      --preserve-root    fail to operate recursively on '/'\n31\t      --reference=RFILE  use RFILE's owner and group rather than specifying\n32\t                         OWNER:GROUP values\n33\t  -R, --recursive        operate on files and directories recursively\n34\t  -H                     if a command line argument is a symbolic link\n35\t                         to a directory, traverse it\n36\t  -L                     traverse every symbolic link to a directory\n37\t                         encountered\n38\t  -P                     do not traverse any symbolic links (default)\n39\t      --help     display this help and exit\n40\t      --version  output version information and exit\n41\t\n42\tOwner is unchanged if missing.  Group is unchanged if missing, but changed\n43\tto login group if implied by a ':' following a symbolic OWNER.\n44\tOWNER and GROUP may be numeric as well as symbolic.\n45\t\n46\tExamples:\n47\t  chown root /u        Change the owner of /u to \"root\".\n48\t  chown root:staff /u  Change the owner of /u to \"root\" and the\n49\t                       group to \"staff\".\n50\t  chown -hR root /u    Change the owner of /u and subfiles to \"root\".\n51\t`\n52\t\n53\tconst versionText = `chown (go-unix-utils) dev\n54\t`\n55\t\n56\ttype symlinkMode int\n57\t\n58\tconst (\n59\t\tsymlinkP symlinkMode = iota\n60\t\tsymlinkH\n61\t\tsymlinkL\n62\t)\n63\t\n64\ttype options struct {\n65\t\tverbose       bool\n66\t\tchanges       bool\n67\t\tsilent        bool\n68\t\treference     string\n69\t\trecursive     bool\n70\t\tnoDereference bool\n71\t\tsymlink       symlinkMode\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\tfunc main() {\n75\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n76\t\n77\t\topts, ownerSpec, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n78\t\tuid, gid := resolveOwnership(opts, ownerSpec)\n79\t\tif len(files) == 0 {\n80\t\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01An2mYVSBpqpTqc5kup5L1i","session_id":"fd2a7807-abd7-4366-bdbe-94cf099e533b","uuid":"4a4921ba-4ba8-4edf-bfbf-c48946add7b7","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:38:17.594Z"}
