{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbnTGfD58wjXH7NZXyXivd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// cmd/chgrp implements srd090-chgrp R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"errors\"\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"os/user\"\n12\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n13\t\t\"strconv\"\n14\t\t\"strings\"\n15\t\n16\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n17\t)\n18\t\n19\tconst helpText = `Usage: chgrp [OPTION]... GROUP FILE...\n20\t  or:  chgrp [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...\n21\tChange the group of each FILE to GROUP.\n22\t\n23\t  -c, --changes          like verbose but report only when a change is made\n24\t  -f, --silent, --quiet  suppress most error messages\n25\t  -v, --verbose          output a diagnostic for every file processed\n26\t      --dereference      affect the referent of each symbolic link (this is\n27\t                         the default), rather than the symbolic link itself\n28\t  -h, --no-dereference   affect symbolic links instead of any referenced file\n29\t      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially (the default)\n30\t      --preserve-root    fail to operate recursively on '/'\n31\t      --reference=RFILE  use RFILE's group rather than specifying a GROUP value\n32\t  -R, --recursive        operate on files and directories recursively\n33\t  -H                     if a command line argument is a symbolic link\n34\t                         to a directory, traverse it\n35\t  -L                     traverse every symbolic link to a directory\n36\t                         encountered\n37\t  -P                     do not traverse any symbolic links (default)\n38\t      --help     display this help and exit\n39\t      --version  output version information and exit\n40\t\n41\tExamples:\n42\t  chgrp staff /u      Change the group of /u to \"staff\".\n43\t  chgrp -hR staff /u  Change the group of /u and subfiles to \"staff\".\n44\t`\n45\t\n46\tconst versionText = `chgrp (go-unix-utils) dev\n47\t`\n48\t\n49\ttype symlinkMode int\n50\t\n51\tconst (\n52\t\tsymlinkP symlinkMode = iota\n53\t\tsymlinkH\n54\t\tsymlinkL\n55\t)\n56\t\n57\ttype options struct {\n58\t\tverbose       bool\n59\t\tchanges       bool\n60\t\tsilent        bool\n61\t\treference     string\n62\t\trecursive     bool\n63\t\tnoDereference bool\n64\t\tsymlink       symlinkMode\n65\t}\n66\t\n67\tfunc main() {\n68\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n69\t\n70\t\topts, group, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n71\t\tgid := resolveGID(opts, group)\n72\t\tgroupLabel := group\n73\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n74\t\t\tgroupLabel = gidToName(gid)\n75\t\t}\n76\t\tif len(files) == 0 {\n77\t\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n78\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: missing operand\")\n79\t\t\t} else {\n80\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: missing operand after '%s'\\n\", group)\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01An2mYVSBpqpTqc5kup5L1i","session_id":"fd2a7807-abd7-4366-bdbe-94cf099e533b","uuid":"21904251-e37b-419c-b341-32578f20a46f","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:38:17.817Z"}
