{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9F8unwfuiWT4ySKexF1hc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd097-who\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/who: Show Who Is Logged On\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD who that differs from GNU who in output format, flag support, and\n6\t  header display. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n7\t  (gwho, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n8\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Show information about currently logged-in users.\n12\t  - G2: Support header display, idle time, and boot time options.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gwho via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default user listing\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must read the utmpx database and print one line per logged-in user showing login name, terminal line, login time, and remote hostname (if available), matching GNU who output format.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When given a FILE argument, must read that file as the utmpx database instead of the system default.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"who am i (or who am I) must print only the entry for the current terminal.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when the utmpx database cannot be read.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Display options\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-H or --heading must print a header line above the output.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-u or --users must show idle time for each user. Idle time is displayed as HH:MM, '.' for active (< 1 minute), or 'old' for > 24 hours.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: \"-b or --boot must show the time of the last system boot.\"\n37\t      - R2.4:\n38\t          text: \"-q or --count must print login names and a count of logged-in users, one name per column.\"\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n47\t      - R3.3:\n48\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n49\t\n50\tnon_goals:\n51\t  - cmd/who does not implement -r (runlevel) or -d (dead processes) on macOS.\n52\t\n53\tacceptance_criteria:\n54\t  - id: AC1\n55\t    criterion: \"who prints logged-in users with terminal and time, matching gwho.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"who -H prints a header line, matching gwho -H.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.1\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"who -b prints boot time, matching gwho -b.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.3\n66\t  - id: AC4\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gwho passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.3\n72\t  - id: AC5\n73\t    criterion: \"cmd/who compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R2.4\n83\t      - R3.1\n84\t      - R3.2\n85\t      - R3.3\n86\t\n87\tpackage_contract:\n88\t  imports:\n89\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n90\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01An2mYVSBpqpTqc5kup5L1i","session_id":"fd2a7807-abd7-4366-bdbe-94cf099e533b","uuid":"2740b863-70ae-4c20-b5b5-ef4c44572e54","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:38:39.298Z"}
