{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R5KfW42FChSfttQf18fsmD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// Implements srd062-touch R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4, R4.1-R4.4.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"fmt\"\n9\t\t\"os\"\n10\t\t\"strconv\"\n11\t\t\"strings\"\n12\t\t\"time\"\n13\t\n14\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n15\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n16\t)\n17\t\n18\ttype options struct {\n19\t\tnoCreate      bool\n20\t\taccessOnly    bool\n21\t\tmodOnly       bool\n22\t\tnoDereference bool\n23\t\tstampStr      string\n24\t\trefFile       string\n25\t\tdateStr       string\n26\t}\n27\t\n28\tfunc main() {\n29\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n30\t\topts, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n31\t\tif err != nil {\n32\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"touch: %s\\n\", err)\n33\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'touch --help' for more information.\\n\")\n34\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n35\t\t}\n36\t\tos.Exit(run(opts, files))\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\tfunc run(opts options, files []string) int {\n40\t\tt, err := resolveTime(opts)\n41\t\tif err != nil {\n42\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"touch: %s\\n\", err)\n43\t\t\treturn 1\n44\t\t}\n45\t\texitCode := 0\n46\t\tfor _, path := range files {\n47\t\t\tif err := touchFile(path, opts, t); err != nil {\n48\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"touch: %s\\n\", err)\n49\t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n50\t\t\t}\n51\t\t}\n52\t\treturn exitCode\n53\t}\n54\t\n55\tfunc resolveTime(opts options) (time.Time, error) {\n56\t\tif opts.refFile != \"\" {\n57\t\t\treturn refFileTime(opts.refFile)\n58\t\t}\n59\t\tif opts.dateStr != \"\" {\n60\t\t\treturn parseDate(opts.dateStr)\n61\t\t}\n62\t\tif opts.stampStr != \"\" {\n63\t\t\treturn parseTimestamp(opts.stampStr)\n64\t\t}\n65\t\treturn time.Now(), nil\n66\t}\n67\t\n68\tfunc refFileTime(path string) (time.Time, error) {\n69\t\tinfo, err := sys.Stat(path)\n70\t\tif err != nil {\n71\t\t\treturn time.Time{}, fmt.Errorf(\n72\t\t\t\t\"failed to get attributes of '%s': %s\", path, sysMsg(err))\n73\t\t}\n74\t\treturn info.ModTime, nil\n75\t}\n76\t\n77\tfunc touchFile(path string, opts options, t time.Time) error {\n78\t\tstatFn := os.Stat\n79\t\tif opts.noDereference {\n80\t\t\tstatFn = os.Lstat\n81\t\t}\n82\t\t_, statErr := statFn(path)\n83\t\tif os.IsNotExist(statErr) {\n84\t\t\tif opts.noCreate {\n85\t\t\t\treturn nil\n86\t\t\t}\n87\t\t\tif !opts.noDereference {\n88\t\t\t\tf, err := os.Create(path)\n89\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n90\t\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cannot touch '%s': %s\", path, sysMsg(err))\n91\t\t\t\t}\n92\t\t\t\tf.Close()\n93\t\t\t}\n94\t\t}\n95\t\tatime, mtime, err := resolveTimestamps(path, opts, t)\n96\t\tif err != nil {\n97\t\t\treturn err\n98\t\t}\n99\t\treturn setTimestamps(path, opts, atime, mtime)\n100\t}\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01An2mYVSBpqpTqc5kup5L1i","session_id":"fd2a7807-abd7-4366-bdbe-94cf099e533b","uuid":"9d7cf358-0dce-43c0-bd48-16f9c1fb204b","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:38:48.054Z"}
